export anchor GamingRGBStyle:
    number: 314
    screen: OpsMonitor
    name: Gaming RGB
    idea: A gamer HUD for the service monitor, with chamfered black panels framed by a cyan to magenta to lime gradient edge, services as a roster of cards with segmented uptime health bars, and terse caps labels.
    base: dark
    palette:
        void: #07080d, the page behind a faint 32px cyan grid
        panel: #10121b, inside every chamfered panel and the style sheet
        panelRaised: #171a26, roster cards, readout boxes and list rows
        ink: #eef1ff, text and figures
        muted: #a3abcb, labels, times and axis ticks
        line: #2a2f45, dividers, grid lines and empty health segments
        cyan: #35e0ff, first stop of the RGB edge, the request line and its glow, links
        magenta: #ff5fdc, middle stop of the RGB edge, the error line, panel title diamonds and the focus glow
        lime: #a6ff5c, last stop of the RGB edge, the p50 line and version tags
        healthy: #8dff6a, Healthy and Resolved words, filled circle and square, health segments
        degraded: #ffc23d, Degraded and Investigating, filled triangle, the dashed p95 line and the SEV 2 tag with near black text
        recovered: #5ee6ff, Recovered word and filled diamond
        firing: #ff6b7d, Firing word and filled octagon
    type:
        Bahnschrift, DIN Alternate, Roboto Condensed, Arial Narrow for text,
        and ui-monospace, Cascadia Mono, Menlo, Consolas for every number,
        service name and time. Base 15px at 1.45. The incident ID is 32px
        mono at 800, readout figures 22px mono at 700, panel titles 13px
        caps tracked 0.2em with a small magenta diamond before them, meta
        12px mono.
    layout:
        A dark top bar with a hexagon BW mark filled with the RGB gradient,
        the Brightwork Ops wordmark in tracked caps, the suite apps Canvas,
        Drive, Code and Ops as caps tabs with a magenta underline on Ops,
        and chips for ENV PRODUCTION and WINDOW 24H plus a search button. A
        2px RGB rule sits under the bar. Below, three columns. Left is a
        300px Service roster panel with five cards, each with a 3px status
        left edge, the service name in mono, a filled status shape and caps
        word, a 20 segment health bar where filled segments show uptime
        above 99 percent, and stats such as UPTIME 99.98% and P95 LATENCY
        182 ms. The centre holds a Throughput panel with three readout boxes
        for Peak, Night low and Now, then a large glowing area chart with a
        cyan PEAK 9,400 tag at the afternoon peak, and beneath it two small
        panels for Error rate and Latency. The right 320px column holds the
        Active incident panel with a big INC-0427, a SEV 2 tag, status,
        opened, owner and two buttons, then an Alert feed and Patch notes
        for deploys with lime version tags. Below 1180px the right column
        becomes a row. Below 760px everything stacks in one column.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px page gutter, 16px between panels, 16px panel padding, 10px between roster cards.
    density: Dense HUD. Roster, three charts and the incident column are visible at once on a laptop.
    corners: No radius. Panels have 14px chamfers at top left and bottom right, roster cards a 10px chamfer at top right, the logo is a hexagon.
    borders: Every panel has a 2px RGB gradient edge made by a gradient behind a clipped inner panel. Cards carry a 3px left status edge, lists use 1px line dividers.
    shadows: None for depth. Only the request line glows with a 4px cyan drop shadow.
    icons:
        Line icons at 1.8 stroke for navigation. Filled status shapes, a
        circle for Healthy, a triangle for Degraded, a diamond for
        Recovered, an octagon for Firing, a square for Resolved and a
        magnifier for Investigating, always beside the word.
    focus: A 2px white outline offset 3px plus a 5px magenta glow ring. Buttons are never clipped so the ring always shows.
    tone: Terse uppercase HUD labels such as Service roster, Alert feed, Patch notes and PEAK 9,400.
